Jahshaka patch 0050 — the irradiance field's host API (and the pass-buffer size
it under-reported), plus the zero auto-multiplier in VctLighting.

SOURCE patch. EVERY TREE MUST RE-RUN `irisgl/scripts/build-ogre.sh` after
pulling this (reset the ogre-next submodule first if it already carries an
earlier revision of any patch: `git -C irisgl/thirdparty/ogre-next checkout -- .
&& git -C irisgl/thirdparty/ogre-next clean -fd`). It OVERLAPS patch 0044
(OgreIrradianceField.h/.cpp) and patch 0037 (OgreIrradianceFieldRaster.cpp,
OgreVctLighting.cpp): it applies on top of them, in stack order, and a
per-patch reverse-check on a tree that carries 0037/0044 reports this one
"unapplied" for those files — judge by content (CLAUDE.md, the overlap blind
spot).

WHY A PATCH AND NOT A WORKAROUND (owner rule, 2026-09-15, ledger §325). Every
item below was a compensation in `irisgl/engine/` for something the pin gets
wrong or keeps private, and each one either depended on an undocumented
ordering inside HlmsPbs, reached into `protected` members from a derived class
of ours, or paid a per-frame cost to avoid a one-line pin defect. Audit
SPECS/audits/ENGINE_WORKAROUNDS_TO_PATCHES_2026-09-15.md, findings F2/F3/F4/F10
and the `unused0` nit.

  1. `IrradianceField::getConstBufferSize()` UNDER-REPORTS BY ONE float4 (F2).
     It returned `sizeof(float) * (4*3 + 4 + 4)` = 80 bytes, while
     `fillConstBufferData` writes an `IrradianceFieldRenderParams` of 96 — a
     float4x3, then numProbesAggregated + 2 pads, then the depth pair, then the
     IRRADIANCE pair — and the struct the generated shader declares
     (`Hlms/Pbs/Any/IrradianceField_piece_ps.any`) is those same 24 floats. So
     HlmsPbs reserved 16 bytes too few for the pass buffer and advanced its
     write pointer by 20 floats after a 24-float write. Upstream's own samples
     simply overrun their pass-buffer map by 16 bytes; with an HlmsListener next
     in line (ours), the listener's first float4 lands on top of
     irradBorderedRes / irradFullWidth / irradInvFullResolution and every
     irradiance UV collapses onto texel 0 — DDGI contributes an almost-black
     constant, with no error anywhere. Engine-side, this was a
     reserve-four-floats-and-skip-them in `FogHlmsListener` that only worked
     because HlmsPbs happens to fill the field's block BEFORE calling the
     listener; it is deleted with this patch.

  2. THE FIELD'S SOURCE SWITCH IS A PUBLIC METHOD NOW (F3).
     `switchToRasterSource( const RasterParams & )` moves a LIVE field from its
     VctLighting source to the raster source without `initialize()` — which
     calls `createTextures()` and blanks both atlases, so a field switched that
     way is born black and re-converges from nothing over thousands of frames
     (six 32x32 renders per probe). The members it needs (`mSettings`,
     `mVctLighting`, `mNumProbesProcessed`, `mIfRaster`,
     `setIrradianceFieldGenParams()`) are all `protected`, i.e. exactly the
     reach-in the rule forbids — `JahIrradianceField`, a derived class of ours
     held and deleted through a NON-VIRTUAL destructor, existed only for this.
     Four read-only accessors come with it, each for a question the class
     already answers internally and nobody outside can ask: `getRasterSource()`
     (its workspace is dropped and re-created on its own when the shadow atlas
     the probe captures name is rebuilt), `getSettings()` (`isRaster()`),
     `getFieldOrigin()`/`getFieldSize()` (the ENLARGED volume — `initialize()`
     grows the caller's volume by one probe block per side and keeps only the
     enlarged value, which is the space `fillConstBufferData` and the raster
     probe cameras work in) and `getNumProbesProcessed()`.

  3. PATCH 0023's C++ HALF, THREE MONTHS LATE (F4). Patch 0023 made the raster
     probe depths grid-relative in the shader and its own header said the C++
     belonged in `IrradianceFieldRaster`: "sets it from mCreator->mFieldSize
     beside mNumProbesParam". It never landed, so the HOST pushed `invFieldSize`
     onto the shared "IrradianceField/CubemapToIfd" job through two string
     lookups (`findComputeJobNoThrow` + `findParameter`) plus a const-buffer
     dirty before EVERY raster update — i.e. thousands of times while a field
     converges — because that job is found by NAME and a second field in the
     process would otherwise leave its own size in force. It is now pushed on
     the line after `numProbes`, which is pushed there for exactly that reason,
     and guarded on the parameter existing so a media tree that predates 0023
     still runs (the host refuses the raster source in that case anyway).

  4. `IrradianceFieldGenParams::unused0` WAS UPLOADED UNINITIALISED on every
     voxel-sourced update (the raster branch memsets the struct; the voxel
     branch writes every member except this one). Zeroed where the rest of the
     struct is written.

  5. `VctLighting::update`'s AUTO MULTIPLIER TURNS "NO LIGHTS" INTO "NO GI"
     (F10). The maximum radiance over the scene's visible lights is 0 in a scene
     with none; the code inverted it unconditionally (+inf), so
     `mInvBakingMultiplier` came out 0 and the shader's
     `blendWeight = blendFade * blend * multiplier` was 0 for every voxel. A
     bound VctLighting also switches the PBS ambient pieces off inside its
     volume, so an ambient-lit scene whose only lamp is switched off went BLACK
     the moment VCT was enabled. The zero case is folded into the branch that
     already exists for "no measurement wanted" (`autoMultiplier == false` →
     `mBakingMultiplier`), which is the same answer the engine was choosing from
     outside — by walking EVERY node in the scene before every injection
     (`OgreScene::hasVctLights`, three call sites) to decide whether to pass
     `autoMultiplier = false`. That walk is deleted with this patch; the three
     call sites pass `true`.

VERIFICATION. `git apply --check` on a tree carrying 0001-0049 and
`git apply --reverse --check` after applying; `build-ogre.sh` re-run in the lane
worktree; `--engine-selftest` byte-identical
(`b55e2d5d03dce4059b71a65f8e61dc4773fb0b048e3de05428aca83cabae0ec7`) — items 1,
2, 4 and 5 are all no-change-by-construction on the shipped default scene
(1: the listener skipped the same four floats it now no longer has to reserve;
2/3: no existing call site; 5: the engine already passed the value this branch
now computes), which the lane measured rather than assumed. The GI suites
(gi.ddgi_*, gi.modes, gi.tiers, gi.budget, gi.coalesce) are the behavioural
gate.

NOTE (second read): of the accessors, the engine uses `switchToRasterSource`,
`getRasterSource` and `getFieldSize`; `getSettings`, `getFieldOrigin` and
`getNumProbesProcessed` have no caller here and are kept as the upstream-facing
shape of the API (a host that owns a field wants all of them).

